From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:35:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/display: Disable PSR2 on the Microsoft Surface Pro 9

On this machine (PCI\VEN_8086&DEV_46A8&SUBSYS_00631414) the display
adapter's registry key under Windows holds PSR2Disable=1 (and
PsrDisableInAc=1), so Windows does not run the LG LP129WT2 panel (EDID
LGD 0x0719) in PSR2.

The VBT enables PSR, and i915 goes on to PSR2 when the sink reports it.
Screen flicker on this machine is a known problem, and the common
workaround, i915.enable_psr=0, also gives up PSR1.

Match what Windows does and disable PSR2 for this subsystem ID, keeping
PSR1.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c
index 7d7db774d..e8822481c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c
@@ -262,6 +262,9 @@ static struct intel_quirk intel_quirks[] = {
 
 	/* Xiaomi Book Pro 14 2026 */
 	{ 0xb081, 0x1d72, 0x2424, quirk_disable_psr2 },
+
+	/* Microsoft Surface Pro 9 (Intel) */
+	{ 0x46a8, 0x1414, 0x0063, quirk_disable_psr2 },
 };
 
 static const struct intel_dpcd_quirk intel_dpcd_quirks[] = {
